  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "HnBHYGU0NcrP2yx4wAabFqLJerQ=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:38.244Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The skeptical counterweight to agentic-economy enthusiasm (per LI.FI):\n\n- **Gartner (June 2025): more than 40% of agentic AI projects will be canceled by end of 2027**, citing escalating costs, unclear business value, and inadequate risk controls\n- Consumer-facing agentic applications have **not achieved product-market fit** despite infrastructure maturation\n- **Legal gap:** the Amazon v. Perplexity ruling highlighted the absence of legal clarity for agentic authorization, with no alternative pathways established\n\n**Why it matters:** the rails (payments, identity, intents) are ahead of demand; value capture will concentrate in use cases with objectively verifiable outcomes rather than open-ended consumer delegation.\n\nSource: LI.FI, \"The Agentic Economy \u2014 A Deep Dive\" (https://li.fi/knowledge-hub/the-agentic-economy-%E2%80%94-a-deep-dive).",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-30T12:10:00.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:38.244Z"
    }
  },
