  {
    "index": 12,
    "hash": "W1NnxKRK7mb86iNdx1AXwPz2d/o=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T10:14:56.813Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The skeptical counterweight to agentic-economy enthusiasm (per LI.FI):\n\n- **Gartner (June 2025): more than 40% of agentic AI projects will be canceled by end of 2027**, citing escalating costs, unclear business value, and inadequate risk controls\n- Consumer-facing agentic applications have **not achieved product-market fit** despite infrastructure maturation\n- **Legal gap:** the Amazon v. Perplexity ruling highlighted the absence of legal clarity for agentic authorization, with no alternative pathways established\n\n**Why it matters:** the rails (payments, identity, intents) are ahead of demand; value capture will concentrate in use cases with objectively verifiable outcomes rather than open-ended consumer delegation.\n\nSource: LI.FI, \"The Agentic Economy \u2014 A Deep Dive\" (https://li.fi/knowledge-hub/the-agentic-economy-%E2%80%94-a-deep-dive).\n\n## Boundary: the bull and bear cases measure different things\nThese two forecasts are routinely read as contradictory and are not. McKinsey sizes a **market** in 2030; Gartner counts **project mortality** by end-2027. A shakeout that kills more than 40% of initiatives while the surviving use cases compound into trillions is the ordinary shape of an infrastructure build-out, not a paradox \u2014 and both sources agree on the mechanism, that the rails are ahead of demand and value concentrates where outcomes are objectively verifiable.\n\nWhat the pair does establish is that **neither number is settled**: the vault should carry them as a scenario range, not as a projection. The discriminating evidence is B2B adoption data in 2027-2028, which is when the two forecasts stop being compatible \u2014 if enterprise orchestration has not compounded by then, the bear case was the base case.\n",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T10:14:56.813Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T10:14:56.813Z"
    }
  }
]